From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_KDA_CHUNKED, production's chunked KDA prompt kernel

ai-engine f2e093ca9 grafted onto the pin stack. glm_kda_chunk.cu/.cuh carry
production's chunked (WY) KDA chain (from glm5_next/cuda/kda_chunk.cu, Apache-2.0,
attribution kept); cuda_kda_chunk.zig sizes it and reads the knob at load;
cuda_kda_block.bodyProfile takes an optional `chunked` prompt and runs the kernel
instead of the serial chain; cuda_forward carries the optional Kernel and passes it
for prompt chunks. States keep and resume on 32-row sub-chunks under the knob.
Knob off: null, the serial chain unchanged.

Pin adaptations: bodyProfile's signature keeps the pin's `o_site` parameter (the L2PF
fork) and gains `chunked` after it, so the call site passes both; the call was rebuilt
to `(..., f.prof, chunked-prompt-or-null, o_site-or-null)` in that order; the later-era
`m.tiled = false` load line is dropped while the Modules field stays, because the
engine assigns it; cuda_kda_chunk's imports resolve at the pin. Comment lines
single-lined, attribution kept.

Gates on pin+0001..0019: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins green for the new .cu files.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0032: glm_l2pf.cu itself and the two fatbin catalog entries the registry's sites need
- 0041: `body` matches bodyProfile's arity, and the L2 prefetch of site o forks after the projections (both lines sit on the bodyProfile this patch rebuilds)
- 0043: glm_l2pf.cu's header on single lines, for the lean gate

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: every TF_* setting this patch reads is a row of platform/environment.zig with a line in docs/environment.md, read through cuda.ovn or environment, never getenv. Row: TF_GLM_OVN_KDA_CHUNKED (flag).
- 5b80e93ac moved the KDA chain to zig/src/cuda/kda.zig: cuda_kda_chunk.zig takes kda.Chain from cuda.kda (the same fields), cuda.zig keeps v1.2.7's `kda = @import("cuda").kda` beside kda_chunk, and cuda_kda_block.bodyProfile gains `chunked` before v1.2.7's o_site.
- cuda_kda_chunk.zig comes whole with this lever (fold-series.md F12): the fold shipped it inside reply-prefill, which this re-seat defers, so the forward reference to cuda.kernels.glm_kda_chunk is gone.
- Not carried: snapGrid() and the core's snapGridNow hook and test in native/cuda_snaps.zig, the any-row era's rule that states keep on 32-row sub-chunks. At v1.2.7 a state is kept only where a chunk ends (the grid or a request start), which the kernel writes as state_out, and a resumed pass starts its chunk where a cold pass cut one.
- Owed by the knob-on check: with TF_GLM_REQUEST_STARTS=1 a chunk can start off the 32-row grid (kda_chunk.chain passes pos % 32), a start the any-row design never let the kernel see.
- source: work/fold/0023-kda-chunked.patch

